#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:1
msgid "Guide to `ros_gz_project_template` for ROS 2 and Gazebo Development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:3
msgid ""
"In this guide, you will learn how to use the `ros_gz_project_template` to "
"create a (recommended) structured workspace or improve your existing "
"workspace for your ROS 2 and Gazebo projects. This template offers a "
"consistent layout, automated build process, and integration with both ROS 2 "
"and Gazebo, enabling you to focus on developing your robotics applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:5
msgid "Installation Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:7
msgid ""
"If you are starting a project, create a new workspace or go to your existing "
"project's source directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:9
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/project_ws/src\n"
"cd ~/project_ws/src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:14
msgid ""
"Directly use the [`ros_gz_project_template` template](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/ros_gz_project_template) and create your project repository on "
"GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:16
msgid "![use_template](tutorials/ros2_integration/use_template.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:16
msgid "use_template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:18
msgid "Or start by cloning the template repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:20
msgid ""
"wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gazebosim/ros_gz_project_template/"
"main/template_workspace.yaml\n"
"vcs import < template_workspace.yaml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:25
msgid "Rename the cloned repository folder to your desired project name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:27
msgid "mv ros_gz_project_template your_project_name\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:31
msgid "Package structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:33
msgid "At this point you'll have the following packages in your project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:35
msgid ""
"`ros_gz_example_application` - holds ROS 2 specific code and configurations. "
"Namely where control, planning or any high level algorithms reside."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:37
msgid ""
" <pre> ├── CMakeLists.txt\n"
" ├── package.xml\n"
" ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>src</b></span>\n"
"     └── ...\n"
" </pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:43
msgid ""
"`ros_gz_example_bringup` - holds launch files and high level utilities, "
"communication bridge between ROS and Gazebo. Any robot or hardware specific "
"configurations go here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:45
msgid ""
" <pre> ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>config</b></span>\n"
" │   ├── ros_gz_example_bridge.yaml\n"
" │   └── diff_drive.rviz\n"
" ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>launch</b></span>\n"
"     └── diff_drive.launch.py\n"
" </pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:52
msgid ""
"`ros_gz_example_description` - holds the SDF description of the simulated "
"system and any other [simulation assets](#accessing-simulation-assets)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:54
msgid ""
" <pre> ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>hooks</b></span>\n"
" │   └── ros_gz_example_description.dsv.in\n"
" ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>models</b></span>\n"
"     ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>diff_drive</b></span>\n"
"         ├── model.config\n"
"         └── model.sdf\n"
" </pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:62
msgid ""
"`ros_gz_example_gazebo` - holds Gazebo specific code and configurations. "
"Namely this is where user-defined worlds and custom system plugins end up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:64
msgid ""
" <pre> ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>include</b></span>\n"
" │   └── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>ros_gz_example_gazebo</b></span>\n"
" │       ├── BasicSystem.hh\n"
" │       └── FullSystem.hh\n"
" ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>src</b></span>\n"
" │   ├── BasicSystem.cc\n"
" │   └── FullSystem.cc\n"
" ├── <span style=\"color:#12488B\"><b>worlds</b></span>\n"
"         └── diff_drive.sdf\n"
" </pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:75
msgid "Accessing Simulation Assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:77
msgid ""
"Simulation assets include your models or robot descriptions in URDF or SDF, "
"meshes and materials files to help visualize different parts of the robot "
"and finally compiling all these elements in a simulated world SDF. Gazebo "
"offers a few different mechanisms for locating those, initializing it's "
"search on `GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH` environment variable, see gz-sim API on "
"[finding resources](https://gazebosim.org/api/sim/8/resources.html) for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:79
msgid ""
"There is a difference in how ROS and Gazebo resolves URIs, that the ROS side "
"can handle `package://` URIs, but by default SDFormat only supports `model://"
"`. Now `libsdformat` can convert `package://` to `model://` URIs. So "
"existing simulation assets can be loaded by \"installing\" the models "
"directory and exporting the model paths to your environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:81
msgid ""
"This can be automated using colcon environment hooks (shell scripts provided "
"by a ROS package) in a [DSV file](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/"
"developer/environment.html?highlight=dsv#dsv-files). Whenever you source the "
"setup file in a workspace these environment hooks are also being sourced. "
"See an [example](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz_project_template/tree/"
"main/ros_gz_example_description/hooks) of prepending the model share path to "
"`GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH` which enables Gazebo to load models from a ROS "
"package using the `model://` URI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:83
msgid "Development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:85
msgid "Choose a ROS and Gazebo [combination](ros_installation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:87
msgid ""
"Note: If you're using a specific and unsupported Gazebo version with ROS 2, "
"you might need to set the `GZ_VERSION` environment variable, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:89
msgid "export GZ_VERSION=garden\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:93
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:95
msgid ""
"cd ~/project_ws\n"
"source /opt/ros/<ROS_DISTRO>/setup.bash\n"
"sudo rosdep init\n"
"rosdep update\n"
"rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -r -i -y --rosdistro "
"<ROS_DISTRO>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:103
msgid "Modify"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:105
msgid ""
"Explore the `src/your_project_name` directory to add/modify the packages "
"associated with your project. There are two primary mechanisms to integrate "
"ROS 2 and Gazebo depending on your application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:107
msgid ""
"Use [ros_gz_bridge](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz) to dynamically "
"connect topics between ROS 2 and Gazebo (which is demonstrated as an example "
"in this template)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:108
msgid "Embed ROS 2 directly in a Gazebo system plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:110
msgid ""
"The main consideration is in choosing the depth of integration is required "
"between ROS and Gazebo. Using the bridge keeps dependencies separate and "
"Gazebo systems don't have to know about ROS. By embedding ROS 2 nodes "
"directly allows accessing the [EntityComponentManager](https://gazebosim.org/"
"api/sim/7/classignition_1_1gazebo_1_1EntityComponentManager.html) within a "
"Gazebo plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:112
msgid "Build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:114
msgid ""
"cd ~/project_ws\n"
"colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=ON\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:119
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:121
msgid "Source the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:123
msgid ". ~/project_ws/install/setup.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:127
msgid "Launch the simulation and visualize in RViz:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:129
msgid ""
"To visualize your robot model and the data generated by your ROS 2 nodes, "
"open a new terminal and launch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_gz_project_template_guide.md:131
msgid "ros2 launch ros_gz_example_bringup diff_drive.launch.py\n"
msgstr ""

